    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0503" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg461"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1862-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 13, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: With reference to the papers in the
                    case of the Labuan, which were recently left at this department by Mr. Stuart, I
                    have the honor to say to you that the Secretary of the Treasury has already
                    given the instructions which were deemed proper with regard to that vessel.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, your lordship’s obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
